[00:20.54]1. The greatest of men was our Lord Jesus Christ;
[00:26.54]By pride or ambition, he was not enticed.
[00:33.54]God’s purpose gave Jesus the prominent role;
[00:41.06]Yet, lowly in heart, he was always whole-souled.
[01:00.76]2. To all who are toiling with troublesome cares,
[01:07.76]He offers to carry the burdens they bear.
[01:14.76]Refreshment they find as the Kingdom they seek.
[01:21.76]With kindness and mildness, he favors the meek.
[01:40.41]3. ‘We all are just brothers,’ our Lord Jesus said.
[01:45.85]In humble submission, we look to our Head.
[01:53.28]The mild and the meek ones to God have great worth;
[02:00.08]He promises they will inherit the earth.